Limitations of NCHILD
- Does not count own children that do not live with the mother
-> divorce, foster care, mothers that work/live elsewhere, children that moved out
-> may be accounted for by restricting to women 18-35
- Includes step-children and adopted children
-> adoption is not a limitation since it still factors in the microeconomic model of the family, and the impact of medicaid coverage is still expected to reduce the cost of having a child
-> same logic may apply to step-children

Limitations of EDUC
- Educational attainment
- Interval between certain years of school is not necessarily equivalent
-> bias against PhD holders?

Limitations of HINSCAID
- People that were once covered by medicaid may have lost coverage 
- Note: demographic changes are not immediate

- look at proportion of:
-> children with divorced parents
-> children under 18 that do not live with their parents

Limitations
- NCHILD
- Discuss endogeneity
- No high-income people with medicaid
-> include general insurance coverage as a dummy variable
-> do noncitizen pregnant women get medicaid?

